{"name":"Terrace View","hex":"#cad0bf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"terrace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat open area on the topmost floor of a building or apartment","A platform that extends outwards from a building."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To provide something with a terrace.","To form something into a terrace."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrace"},{"term":"view","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Visual perception.\nThe act of seeing or looking at something.","The act of seeing or looking at something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To look at.","To regard in a stated way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/view"}],"entries":[{"title":"Citygarden","blocks":[{"text":"Citygarden is an urban park and sculpture garden in St. Louis, Missouri owned by the City of St. Louis but maintained by the Gateway Foundation. It is located between Eighth, Tenth, Market, and Chestnut streets, in the city's \"Gateway Mall\" area. Before being converted to a garden and park, the site comprised two empty blocks of grass. Citygarden was dedicated on June 30, 2009, and opened one day later, on July 1, 2009."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Citygarden_limestone_wall_sign.jpg/330px-Citygarden_limestone_wall_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citygarden"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Citygarden_looking_across_9th_Street_to_8th_Street.jpg/500px-Citygarden_looking_across_9th_Street_to_8th_Street.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Citygarden_looking_across_9th_Street_to_8th_Street.jpg/1280px-Citygarden_looking_across_9th_Street_to_8th_Street.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","s